  Bmp1:
    'Bmp1 is a metalloproteinase that processes extracellular matrix and procollagens rather than a classic Smad activating ligand, so modeling decisions differ from other Bmps. Global disruption hits matrix maturation hard and can limit viability, pushing many matrix biology teams toward conditional alleles. Fibroblast or osteoblast restricted deletion isolates tissue autonomous processing defects. Knockin catalytic mutants distinguish protease function from any residual BMP like signaling hypotheses. Humanized Bmp1 supports antibody and inhibitor programs that engage human BMP1 domains selectively.',
  Bmp10:
    'Developmental modeling of Bmp10 starts from TGF beta family Smad signaling in patterning and fibrosis. Partner genetics reduce redundancy risk that single morphogen knockouts can leave behind. Global knockout often disrupts early patterning, so conditional deletion of Bmp10 after the critical window is usually required for adult questions. Match Cre geography to the field that actually expresses Bmp10 in your system. Transgenic overexpression tests gain of morphogen tone when ectopic signaling is the disease idea around Bmp10. If sibling morphogens may compensate, plan dual conditional strategies rather than trusting a single locus null.',
  Bmp15:
    'Bmp15 is an oocyte derived TGF beta family member that partners with Gdf9 in follicular control. Species differences in dosage sensitivity make mouse modeling strategy especially important for translating human ovarian biology. Global knockout phenotypes in mice can be milder than sheep or human loss, so knockin humanization of Bmp15 is often more informative than a simple null. Conditional oocyte deletion still clarifies stage specific requirements. Programs building fertility biologics frequently request humanized Bmp15 for epitope matched in vivo assays.',
  Bmp2:
    'Bmp2 is a potent osteoinductive morphogen also active in heart valve and craniofacial development. Complete loss is embryonic lethal with cardiac failure, so almost every adult bone or valve study needs conditional knockout. Osteoblast, chondrocyte, or endothelial Cre drivers define whether Bmp2 acts locally during fracture repair or valve remodeling. Knockin and transgenic overexpression models remain standard for osteoinduction and heterotopic ossification research. Humanized Bmp2 matters when recombinant human BMP2 biologics or neutralizing antibodies require matched epitopes in the mouse host.',
  Bmp3:
    'Bmp3 (BMP3) contributes to TGF beta family Smad signaling in patterning and fibrosis. Transgenic overexpression tests gain of morphogen tone when ectopic signaling is the disease idea around Bmp3. Knockout, conditional knockout, knockin, and humanized alleles cover most morphogen program escalations at Bmp3. Tissue restricted Cre helps show whether Bmp3 acts from epithelium, mesenchyme, or an organizing center. If embryogenesis collapses the cohort, do not force a conventional KO for an adult endpoint at Bmp3. Partner genetics reduce redundancy risk that single morphogen knockouts can leave behind.',
  Bmp4:
    'Bmp4 patterns extraembryonic mesoderm, lens, and limb, and later influences fibrosis and metabolic tissues. Null embryos die early, making floxed Bmp4 the workhorse for postnatal questions. Tissue restricted deletion in lung, kidney, or adipose isolates organ specific BMP tone without gastrulation collapse. Point mutant knockins that reduce but do not erase Bmp4 better mimic hypomorphic human syndromes. Humanized alleles support programs comparing mouse versus human BMP4 for antibody and ligand trap development.',
  Bmp5:
    'Bmp5 contributes to skeletal patterning and soft tissue morphology, with classic spontaneous mutants historically guiding the field. Engineered knockout and conditional alleles now give cleaner genetics than older stocks for quantitative bone and ear studies. Conditional deletion helps when developmental skeletal phenotypes obscure adult remodeling questions. Knockin disease alleles recreate human BMP5 linked traits more faithfully than nulls alone. Humanized models appear when therapeutic antibodies need human BMP5 extracellular sequence in vivo.',
  Bmp6:
    'Bmp6 regulates iron homeostasis through hepcidin induction and also contributes to joint and bone biology. Unlike several BMP siblings, global Bmp6 loss is often compatible with adult cohorts focused on anemia of inflammation and hepcidin pharmacology. Conditional liver or macrophage deletion still helps when you need to separate hepatic Bmp6 from skeletal sources. Knockin alleles that alter mature ligand processing support mechanism studies beyond simple nulls. Humanized Bmp6 is relevant for hepcidin pathway biologics tuned to human BMP6.',
  Bmp7:
    'Bmp7 is known for kidney development and antifibrotic signaling in adult kidney and eye. Global knockout causes severe renal and ocular defects, so conditional strategies dominate adult CKD and fibrosis pipelines. Tubule or interstitial Cre drivers clarify whether Bmp7 loss worsens fibrosis through epithelial or stromal routes. Knockin and transgenic replacement models test whether restoring Bmp7 tone after injury is sufficient for repair. Humanized Bmp7 lines help evaluate clinical BMP7 analogs and antibodies in a sequence matched context.',
  Bmp8a:
    'Bmp8a participates in spermatogenesis and thermogenic adipose biology, linking reproductive and metabolic modeling choices. Global loss can produce measurable germline and metabolic phenotypes, yet tissue restricted floxed alleles clarify which organ drives the readout. Germ cell versus somatic Cre drivers are especially important in testis studies. Knockin and transgenic approaches test gain of Bmp8a in brown fat activation hypotheses. Humanized Bmp8a supports translational work when human BMP8A sequence diverges at antibody epitopes.',
  Bmp8b:
    'Bmp8b (BMP8B) contributes to TGF beta family Smad signaling in patterning and fibrosis. Hypomorphic knockins can mimic human BMP8B dosage syndromes better than complete nulls when partial function is the clinical picture. Antibody programs against human BMP8B should prioritize humanized Bmp8b once the conditional plan looks viable. If embryogenesis collapses the cohort, do not force a conventional KO for an adult endpoint at Bmp8b. Knockin reporters map source domains during development without removing ligand activity at Bmp8b. Timed inducible alleles separate embryonic patterning failure from adult repair involving Bmp8b.',
  Braf:
    'Labs ask about Braf when the question centers on MAPK kinase activity common in melanoma and related cancers. Crossing Braf alleles to a pathway partner often says more than studying the gene alone. A whole body knockout works when the allele is viable. If early lethality shows up, a floxed Braf line with tissue or inducible Cre is usually the safer route. A floxed line plus a well chosen Cre is often enough to get usable signaling cohorts. Reporter knockins map where Braf is expressed without wiping out every transcript.',
  Brca1:
    'Brca1 maintains genome integrity through homologous recombination repair. Pathogenic variants raise breast and ovarian cancer risk, so mouse models support BRCA directed therapy development and synthetic lethality screens. Tissue restricted knockouts help isolate mammary biology without early embryonic complications that can complicate whole body loss. Humanized alleles are useful when antibodies are human epitope selective. Well chosen floxed lines shorten the path from genetics to pharmacology cohorts.',
  Brca2:
    'Brca2 works alongside Brca1 in DNA repair and drives similar clinical risk profiles. Engineered mice test platinum sensitivity, PARP combinations, and resistance mechanisms that emerge after treatment. Conditional approaches keep lethality manageable while still yielding tumors with clear repair deficits. Models are frequently crossed to tissue specific promoters so investigators can align organ site with the human syndrome.',
