  Foxp3:
    'Foxp3 defines regulatory T cell identity. Engineered mice clarified how Treg loss unleashes autoimmunity and how targeted modulation might treat cancer without catastrophic inflammation. Cre lines under Foxp3 regulatory elements are reference tools across immunology. Conditional timing experiments separate development from homeostasis in tolerance.',
  Fst:
    'Fst is requested for projects centered on BMP antagonist and morphogen buffer activity. If sibling morphogens may compensate, plan dual conditional strategies rather than trusting a single locus null. Knockin reporters map source domains during development without removing ligand activity at Fst. Patterning genes reward spatial and temporal control more than blunt systemic deletion. Partner genetics reduce redundancy risk that single morphogen knockouts can leave behind. Global knockout often disrupts early patterning, so conditional deletion of Fst after the critical window is usually required for adult questions.',
  Fus:
    'Fus comes up when programs need clean genetics around neurodegeneration biology spanning proteostasis and neuronal stress without losing animals before aging windows open. For antibody and ASO programs, human sequence at Fus closes a gap that mouse only genetics leave open. Aged cohorts should drive whether you need a strong null or a milder hypomorphic knockin at Fus. Prefer cKO or disease knockins for adult brain questions. Use humanized alleles when the drug is sequence selective for FUS. Humanized Fus helps when pathology depends on human specific isoforms or aggregation sequences in FUS.',
