  Gdf9:
    'Gdf9 is an oocyte secreted factor essential for follicular development, making reproductive biology the primary use case. Global knockout yields female infertility with clear ovarian histology, which is often sufficient for mechanism work. Conditional oocyte specific strategies still help when you need temporal control across follicle stages. Knockin variants that model human GDF9 infertility mutations support genotype aligned pharmacology. Humanized Gdf9 becomes important for biologics and diagnostics that bind human GDF9 but not the mouse protein.',
