  Ihh:
    'Ihh coordinates chondrocyte proliferation and osteoblast recruitment at the growth plate, which makes skeletal biology the primary modeling decision. Whole body knockout arrests endochondral ossification early, so most bone repair and osteoarthritis studies prefer floxed Ihh with cartilage or osteoblast Cre drivers. Conditional timing also separates embryonic growth plate failure from adult remodeling questions in fracture healing. Knockin point mutants support programs that chase human IHH skeletal dysplasias rather than simple loss of function. Humanized alleles become relevant when biologics or decoy receptors discriminate human versus mouse ligand interfaces.',
  Ikbkb:
    'Ikbkb is the mouse form of human IKBKB and takes part in intracellular signaling that links extracellular cues to growth. A floxed line plus a well chosen Cre is often enough to get usable signaling cohorts. Related pathway members can mask a single locus knockout, so dual conditional crosses are worth planning if redundancy is likely. For antibody work, a human exon knockin at Ikbkb can avoid false negatives from sequence drift. Many groups flox Ikbkb first, then keep a null only if they need a severity benchmark or a rescue cross.',
  Ikbke:
    'Ikbke supports immune signaling in host defense, tolerance, or inflammation, so people ask which cell type should lose or gain function. We can quote KO, cKO, knockin, and humanized paths for Ikbke so viability and epitope needs stay aligned. Deleting Ikbke in T cells, B cells, myeloid cells, or epithelium helps pin down which compartment drives the phenotype. If the assay is antibody blockade of IKBKE, plan humanized Ikbke early and use mouse nulls to show pathway need. Checkpoint or cytokine partner crosses are common when a single Ikbke mutant understates combination biology.',
  Ikbkg:
    'Ikbkg (IKBKG) sits in intracellular signaling that links extracellular cues to growth, so allele choice tends to matter early. Related pathway members can mask a single locus knockout, so dual conditional crosses are worth planning if redundancy is likely. Whether you need loss of function, a disease allele, or human sequence at Ikbkg usually settles the design. Crossing Ikbkg alleles to a pathway partner often says more than studying the gene alone. Signaling readouts, tumor latency, and drug response each favor different allele classes at Ikbkg.',
